# Keep shell scripts LF-only so they stay runnable after a clone on
# Linux/macOS/WSL, regardless of the committer's platform or core.autocrlf.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the workflows. Today every `run:` in them is a single line,
# which YAML strips the line ending from either way — but a multi-line `run: |`
# block committed with CRLF would carry a trailing \r into each command on the
# Linux leg, and "command not found: apt-get\r" is a confusing way to learn this.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
